{
  "root_node": "source.raw.orders",
  "cause": "upstream_data",
  "action": "escalate",
  "evidence": "The stg_orders model failed contract validation because its order_date column is defined as DATE in the contract but the source raw.orders.o_orderdate column is VARCHAR. Profiling shows 600 out of 15,000 rows contain values (e.g., \"unknown\") that cannot be converted to DATE, making the conversion lossy. According to team policy, a type/format change can only be patched if lossless, which is not the case here. Therefore the issue originates in the raw source data, and the appropriate response is to escalate to the source owner."
}
